# Line endings, and the one place where a byte is a promise.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository is developed on machines with `core.autocrlf=true`. Git then
# rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. For source that is fine. For a file whose
# *hash* is published as a promise, it is not.
#
# `site/vendor/three-r128.min.js` has its sha512 pinned in the `VENDOR` table of
# `scripts/check-csp.mjs`, checked against the SRI that cdnjs publishes for r128.
# Measured 2026-08-19: a fresh checkout on Windows produced 603451 bytes where the
# committed blob has 603445 — six LF→CRLF conversions, and the hash stops matching.
#
# CORRECTION, 2026-08-19, found by the Tubarão-branco in clean water: the first
# version of this comment said the page carries `integrity=` and that **the browser
# refuses to execute the script**. Measured: there are **zero** `integrity=`
# attributes under `site/`. The file is loaded same-origin by plain `<script src>`.
# The consequence of the drift is that `check-csp` goes red on a fresh Windows
# clone — loud, in CI and in the hook — not that the browser silently drops it.
# The claim was inferred from the presence of a hash in the gate and written as if
# it had been observed. `-text` is still right; the reason given was not.
#
# The header of `check-csp.mjs` already names this line-ending trap for
# inline-script hashes and avoids it there. The vendor file sat inside the same
# trap unguarded.
#
# `-text` means: never translate line endings, on any platform, in either
# direction. It is the only setting under which a pinned hash survives a clone.

# Solidity: o byte É a procedência.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Os artefatos em `contracts/out/` registram o keccak256 de cada fonte que entrou
# na compilação — e é por esse hash que se prova que o `.sol` deste repositório é
# o mesmo que gerou o bytecode vivo na Polygon. Medido em 2026-08-19:
#
#   contracts/src/TriviuCerca.sol   disco  28658 bytes  0x0e52d5aa…  BATE
#                                   clone  29238 bytes  0x3ca9b937…  DIVERGE
#
# 580 conversões LF→CRLF, e o hash deixa de bater. Quem clonasse recompilaria e
# obteria uma fonte que o artefato do contrato vivo não reconhece — num repositório
# cuja capa diz "Open source. Verifiable math." A prova de procedência só existe se
# o byte atravessar o clone intacto.

*.sol            -text

# O QR carrega uma promessa.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `site/selo/qr-contrato.svg` decodifica para o endereco do TriviuExecutor no
# explorador, e essa decodificacao e a UNICA prova de que o codigo leva onde a
# cena do selo e a faixa da home dizem que leva.
#
# Ele nao estava aqui, e em 2026-08-20 o N2 do Tubarao-branco comparou o sha256
# do disco contra o do commit e obteve divergencia:
#
#     disco   9356c996af8fd7b5   4404 bytes   8 CRLF
#     commit  57dc8ca59ce3a944   4396 bytes   0 CRLF
#
# Nao era nada: so quebra de linha, e o `<path>` com os modulos escuros — o que
# o leitor de QR de fato le — e byte-identico. Mas o juiz esteve a um passo de
# declarar que a prova nao valia mais, e QUALQUER conferencia futura por hash
# devolveria o mesmo susto.
#
# O dano nao e ao QR. E a verificabilidade dele. `-text` torna a conferencia por
# hash uma resposta em vez de uma investigacao.
site/selo/qr-contrato.svg  -text

site/vendor/**   -text
*.min.js         -text
*.woff2          -text
*.png            -text
*.jpg            -text
*.ico            -text

# Hooks are executed by sh. A CRLF after `#!/usr/bin/env sh` makes the kernel
# look for an interpreter named "sh\r", which does not exist. LF, always.
.githooks/**     text eol=lf
